#+TITLE: Require native COM quiescence before opening the job DWG
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: native-cad-validation
#+BRANCH: codex/alfe-com-job-drawing

* Evidence
SCHME !339 BricsCAD jobs 564960, 564958 and 565290 lose their application
before READY, at app.HWND, after Documents.Open/Activate. Windows events for
564960 record BricsCAD faults in KERNELBASE.dll and ntdll.dll. The bridge opens
the requested DWG immediately after CreateObject responds, and only then
captures the owned process. The exact native crash cause remains unconfirmed.

* Correction under qualification
Both COM emitters require GetAcadState().IsQuiescent before Documents.Open,
with a bounded 30-second check. Capture the exact created application's window
process identity before opening the file, so a file-open crash does not erase
the ownership evidence. No attach/replacement instance lookup and no fallback
to a blank drawing. A failed readiness check remains a startup failure.

* References
- https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2024/KOR/AutoCAD-ActiveX-Reference/files/GUID-820F93B4-7B83-4708-8E21-0D43D7D1C828.htm
- https://developer.bricsys.com/bricscad/help/en_US/V9/DevRef/source/IDR_VBA_Objects953.htm

* Native qualification (2026-11-17, PF5S26BT, master 3476a558)

The gate works as specified: it refuses to open the job drawing while the
application is not quiescent, and alfe reports a startup failure (exit 69).
verify:epure-lifecycle:windows, jobs 18100605195 and 18102246438 (the second
after pjb dismissed the dialogs by hand): every native automation row --
AutoCAD and BricsCAD, with and without the EPURE plug-in -- ends with

: ERROR COM bridge: COM application did not become quiescent before opening the job drawing

(bridge exit 4, ATTACHED=0 CREATED=1); the simulated lifecycle cases pass.
pjb saw what holds the applications busy: the SCHMS "Nouveautes" dialog and
EPURE startup dialogs (plus one BricsCAD crash report). They come back on
every start, so dismissing them once does not help. BricsCAD batch with EPURE
stays at BOOTING until killed at 420 s (forced=True), and crashed with
0xC000041D in the first run.

Next: the runner's CAD profiles must not show startup dialogs (SCHMS/EPURE
"don't show again" or plug-in settings), then rerun
verify:epure-lifecycle:windows. The issue stays open until a native run
passes.
